# Purpose Code Mapping

## Objective

Explore how purpose-code classification affects transaction processing,
merchant onboarding and compliance automation.

## Core Hypothesis

Purpose-code selection should move from a static compliance field toward
an intelligent transaction-classification layer.

Instead of asking:

"What purpose code should the merchant select?"

a technology platform could ask:

"What is the underlying economic activity?"

and use transaction metadata, invoice descriptions and merchant information
to suggest the appropriate regulatory classification.

## Initial Mapping

| Business Activity | Example | Purpose Code | Compliance Consideration |
|---|---|---|---|
| Software export | SaaS/software development | P0802* | Export documentation |
| IT-enabled services | BPO/data analytics | P0806* | Export documentation |
| Management consulting | Advisory services | P1007* | Export documentation |
| Advertising | Digital advertising | P1101* | Export documentation |
| Healthcare | Telehealth services | P0014* | Sector-specific documentation |
| R&D | Technology research | P0801* | Export documentation |

*Codes should be independently validated against the current RBI master
direction before being used operationally.

## Technology Opportunity

Potential automation:

Invoice / Contract
       ↓
Natural Language Classification
       ↓
Candidate Purpose Code
       ↓
Regulatory Rule Engine
       ↓
Human / Compliance Validation
       ↓
Transaction Processing
